From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 11:07:34 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] msm8996-common: install init.recovery.qcom.rc at the ramdisk
 root

prebuilt_root without install_in_root installs to the partition subdir, so the
file landed at /system/init.recovery.qcom.rc. The generic init.rc imports
/init.recovery.${ro.hardware}.rc from the root, which is also where 22.2 had
it, so it would never have been read and the symlink and sys.usb.configfs it
sets would still have been missing.

Caught by unpacking the built recovery ramdisk rather than trusting that the
module installed somewhere useful.
---
 recovery/Android.bp | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/recovery/Android.bp b/recovery/Android.bp
index 54b2eb80..36437576 100644
--- a/recovery/Android.bp
+++ b/recovery/Android.bp
@@ -11,4 +11,8 @@ prebuilt_root {
     name: "init.recovery.qcom.rc",
     src: "root/init.recovery.qcom.rc",
     recovery: true,
+    // Without this it lands in the partition subdir, i.e. /system/init.recovery.qcom.rc, and the
+    // generic init.rc imports /init.recovery.${ro.hardware}.rc from the ramdisk root, so it would
+    // never be read. Same pair bootable/recovery/fonts uses.
+    install_in_root: true,
 }
